== Method chosen by the tester (no steps in the DB)
For each copper SFP fitted in the x230, bring its link up at every speed the pair can run and read the x230's status:
  autonegotiation restricted to one speed (`speed auto 100`, `speed auto 10`, `speed auto 1000`), a fixed `speed 1000`, and
  back to `speed auto`; where the partner is a switch, also a forced (no autoneg) 100/full on both ends.
  Pass: "connected" at the configured speed and full duplex within 25 s, no "% " error from the x230, and the port back at
  a-full a-1000 at the end.
Copper pluggables in the x230 (show system pluggable, 18:42 and show system pluggable detail, 18:53, all "1000BASE-T"):
  port1.0.1 AT-SPTXa A04906R191400072  <-> AR4050S port1.0.2 (fixed copper; 4050 side shutdown at the start)
  port1.0.2 AT-SPTX  A03245R112100715  <-> stack port1.0.2  (IE520 AT-SPTXa, static-channel-group 2)
  port1.0.3 AT-SPTX  A03245R084100100  <-> stack port1.0.17 (IE520 AT-SPTXa A04906F202000099)
  port1.0.5 AT-SPTXc A10217F241400236  <-> tb470 eth3 (host NIC, 10/100/1000 autoneg; untouched)
