== Summary
PROVEN on the x230v2-28GS:
  AT-SPTXa (port1.0.1) 10 / 100 / 1000 full (autoneg) and fixed 1000 full, against the AR4050S.
  AT-SPTXc (port1.0.5) 10 / 100 / 1000 full (autoneg) and fixed 1000 full, against tb470 eth3.
  AT-SPTX  (port1.0.2, port1.0.3) 100 / 1000 full (autoneg), fixed 1000 full, and forced 100/full (port1.0.3).
NOT MEASURABLE here: AT-SPTX at 10 Mb/s -- both SPTX ports face IE520 AT-SPTXa ports, which reject 10 Mb/s
  ("% port1.0.17: Unsupported speed/duplex combination port1.0.17"). It needs a 10-capable partner on an SPTX (e.g. move an
  SPTX into port1.0.1 against the 4050, or the 4050 cable onto port1.0.2/1.0.3) -- a recable, the Test Engineer's.
No "% " error from the x230 for any speed; every link back at a-full a-1000.

Run: clean.
VERDICT: PASS -- x230 copper SFPs link full at every speed the bench can drive: SPTXa and SPTXc at 10/100/1000 (auto) + fixed 1000, SPTX at 100/1000 + forced 100/full; SPTX at 10 not measurable (the IE520 partner rejects 10)
